, Canada, the United Kingdom, Ireland, Australia, New Zealand, Western Europe, the Middle East, Latin America, South Africa, and Asia. It operates through Platform and Products segments. The company offers connected machines, accessories, and materials for users to create personalized birthday cards, mugs, T-shirts, and large-scale interior decorations. Its connected machines, which are used to cut, write, score, and create decorative effects on paper, adhesive vinyl, iron-on vinyl, wood, and leather, comprise Cricut Joy family, Cricut Explore family, Cricut Maker family, and Cricut Venture. The company also provides Cricut Design Space, a cloud-based software that integrates with connected machines to enable users to create and work on projects across desktop and mobile devices; Cricut Access and Cricut Access Premium subscription offerings; and in-app purchases of images, fonts, and projects. In addition, it offers a range of accessories and materials, such as Cricut EasyPress, Cricut Mug Press, hand tools, machine replacement tools and blades, and project materials, such as vinyl and iron-on. Further, the company provides craft, DIY, home d\u00e9cor products, and extensions. It offers its products through its third-party brick-and-mortar and online retail partners; and its website cricut.com, as well as through a network of distributors. Cricut, Inc. was formerly known as Provo Craft & Novelty, Inc. and changed its name to Cricut, Inc. in March 2018. The company was incorporated in 1969 and is headquartered in South Jordan, Utah.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Ashish  Arora | CEO, President & Director | Age 57 | Compensation: $8.0M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 700 people. Revenue per employee of $1.0M ranks in the top quartile among Technology peers, with revenue falling 14%/yr across its filed history. Stock-based compensation of $50K per employee reflects an ownership culture. CEO compensation is 8\u00d7 revenue per employee (modest relative to workforce productivity). Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (10/10).","financial_summary":["Cricut, Inc. is a small-cap technology business with a $1.9B market cap on $709M of annual revenue.","The top line has compounded at -7% over the past three years, and a shrinking top line is the hardest headwind any business can overcome.","Returns on capital run at 26% against a 9% cost of capital \u2014 a 16-point spread that is the clearest signature of an economic moat, with gross margins sitting at 45%.","On the balance sheet, the balance sheet carries net cash, which is the gold standard: the business never has to make desperate decisions in a bad year.","Management returns a meaningful 12.1% of market cap to owners through dividends and buybacks, a strong signal of disciplined capital allocation, and insiders hold 9.1% of the shares."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Price sits 132% above estimated fair value \u2014 no margin of safety left, and the cushion against estimate error has been bid away (confirmed by 1 other valuation measure)","sev":"red","cat":"valuation","magnitude":1.3214140796662135},{"text":"Revenue growth in the bottom decile of Technology peers \u2014 losing share inside the profit pool","sev":"red","cat":"growth"},{"text":"Fragmented industry with below-average profit capture \u2014 no moat to protect margins","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Volatile returns on capital suggest the moat is narrower than a snapshot ROIC implies","sev":"amber","cat":"moat"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (10.6% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the other way","sev":"amber","cat":"sentiment"},{"text":"Insiders are net sellers (100% sell ratio, net $8.2M) \u2014 the people closest to the business are reducing their personal stake","sev":"amber","cat":"insider"},{"text":"Technology sector lagging the market significantly, underperforming by 9% over 3 months","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Technology ETF trading well below its long-term trend","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Elevated sector volatility (52% annualized) adds uncertainty","sev":"amber","cat":"sector"},{"text":"Cybersecurity liability and talent cost inflation \u2014 a single breach can erase years of goodwill, and the war for engineering talent compresses margins even at scale.","sev":"amber","cat":"thesis_risk"}],"sector_tailwinds":["Piotroski score 7/9 \u2014 financials improving across profitability, leverage and efficiency","Altman Z comfortably in the safe zone \u2014 a fortress balance sheet on this measure","Healthy payout ratio leaves room for both dividend growth and reinvestment"],"news_headlines":[{"title":"Precision Trading with Cricut Inc. (CRCT) Risk Zones","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/11/Precision_Trading_with_Cricut_Inc._CRCT_Risk_Zones_112526042001_1795598401.html","date":"2026-11-25","timestamp":1795598401.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":-0.494,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"CRCT Stock Rises 58% in 3 Months: Here's What Investors Should Know","source":"zacks.com","link":"https://www.zacks.com/stock/news/3032594/crct-stock-rises-58-in-3-months-here-s-what-investors-should-know?cid=CS-ZC-FT-analyst_blog%7Cprice_surge_%2F_plunge-3032594","date":"2026-11-19","timestamp":1795100940.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.0,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":[]},{"title":"Cricut (NASDAQ:CRCT) CEO Sells $600,600.00 in Stock","source":"thelincolnianonline.com","link":"https://www.thelincolnianonline.com/2026/11/16/cricut-nasdaqcrct-ceo-sells-600600-00-in-stock.html","date":"2026-11-16","timestamp":1794821117.0,"origin":"tiingo","sentiment":0.772,"tier":0,"scope":"company","tags":["leadership"]},{"title":"Trading Systems Reacting to (CRCT) Volatility","source":"news.stocktradersdaily.com","link":"https://news.stocktradersdaily.com/news_release/8/Trading_Systems_Reacting_to_CRCT_Volatility_111526061201_1794741121.html","date":"2026-11-1